### Auth Service API Examples

### 1. Health Check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/health

###

### 2. Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 3. Register another user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "securepass456"
}

###

### 4. Verify email (remplacez tokenId et t avec les vraies valeurs reçues par email/console)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/verify?tokenId=VOTRE_TOKEN_ID&t=VOTRE_TOKEN_CLEAR

###

### 5. Login - Successful login (après avoir vérifié l'email)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 6. Login - Failed (Wrong Password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###

### 7. Login - Failed (Email Not Verified)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "securepass456"
}

###

### 8. Login - Failed (User Not Found)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 9. Check H2 Database Console
# Ouvrir dans le navigateur: http://localhost:8080/h2-console
# JDBC URL: jdbc:h2:mem:authdb
# Username: sa
# Password: (laisser vide)
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "password123",
  "provider": "LOCAL"
}

### 13. Register - Validation Error (Short Password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "12345",
  "provider": "LOCAL"
}

### 14. Register - Duplicate Username
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john_doe",
  "email": "different@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "provider": "LOCAL"
}

### 15. Register - Duplicate Email
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "different_user",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "provider": "LOCAL"
}

###
